{
  "_comment": [
    "Language-neutral conformance corpus for the QTerm runtime (issue #159).",
    "",
    "Three published packages implement the same builder API and must agree:",
    "quiltlang (crates.io), quilt-python (PyPI) and quilt-wasm (npm). Each has a",
    "thin runner that walks these cases against its native API, so a divergence",
    "is a test failure rather than something a user discovers.",
    "",
    "A term is a tagged object:",
    "  {\"leaf\": {\"tag\": t, \"text\": s}}   {\"sym\": s}   {\"name\": s}",
    "  {\"qlift\": v}                        {\"qlift_html\": v}",
    "  {\"tb\": {\"tag\": t, \"steps\": [...]}}",
    "  {\"quote\"|\"unquote\": {tag, index, lang, term, cmds}}",
    "A step is {\"w\": s} | {\"c\": term} | {\"e\": term} | {\"p\": s} | \"n\" | \"x\".",
    "A cmd is  {\"write\": s} | {\"push\": s} | \"NL\" | \"POP\" | \"HOLE\".",
    "",
    "`runtimes` narrows a case to the implementations that have the API; omit it",
    "to mean all three. Every narrowing needs a `why`, so a gap is a recorded",
    "decision and not an accident.",
    "",
    "The governing law for lift is ↓(↑(x)) == x: ↑ maps a value to a term whose",
    "code evaluates back to it. These cases compare coparse() text, which cannot",
    "see that law directly — checking it needs the reduce backends, so it lives",
    "in the nightly job. A case that records behaviour known to *violate* the law",
    "carries a `deviation` field: it is pinned so a change is noticed, not because",
    "it is right."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "leaf",
      "term": {
        "leaf": {
          "tag": "integer_literal",
          "text": "42"
        }
      },
      "coparse": "42"
    },
    {
      "name": "sym",
      "term": {
        "sym": "+"
      },
      "coparse": "+"
    },
    {
      "name": "name",
      "term": {
        "name": "foo"
      },
      "coparse": "foo"
    },
    {
      "name": "builder_binary_expression",
      "term": {
        "tb": {
          "tag": "binary_expression",
          "steps": [
            {
              "c": {
                "leaf": {
                  "tag": "integer_literal",
                  "text": "1"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "w": " "
            },
            {
              "c": {
                "sym": "+"
              }
            },
            {
              "w": " "
            },
            {
              "c": {
                "leaf": {
                  "tag": "integer_literal",
                  "text": "2"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "coparse": "1 + 2"
    },
    {
      "name": "builder_empty_tag_only",
      "term": {
        "tb": {
          "tag": "block",
          "steps": [
            {
              "w": "{}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "coparse": "{}"
    },
    {
      "name": "builder_newline",
      "term": {
        "tb": {
          "tag": "block",
          "steps": [
            {
              "w": "a"
            },
            "n",
            {
              "w": "b"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "coparse": "a\nb"
    },
    {
      "name": "builder_push_pop_prefix",
      "term": {
        "tb": {
          "tag": "block",
          "steps": [
            {
              "w": "{"
            },
            {
              "p": "    "
            },
            "n",
            {
              "w": "body"
            },
            "x",
            "n",
            {
              "w": "}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "coparse": "{\n    body\n}"
    },
    {
      "name": "builder_nested_children",
      "term": {
        "tb": {
          "tag": "call",
          "steps": [
            {
              "c": {
                "name": "print"
              }
            },
            {
              "w": "("
            },
            {
              "c": {
                "tb": {
                  "tag": "binary_expression",
                  "steps": [
                    {
                      "c": {
                        "leaf": {
                          "tag": "integer_literal",
                          "text": "1"
                        }
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "w": "+"
                    },
                    {
                      "c": {
                        "leaf": {
                          "tag": "integer_literal",
                          "text": "2"
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "w": ")"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "coparse": "print(1+2)"
    },
    {
      "name": "builder_emit",
      "term": {
        "tb": {
          "tag": "block",
          "steps": [
            {
              "w": "{"
            },
            {
              "e": {
                "leaf": {
                  "tag": "expression_statement",
                  "text": "a;"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "e": {
                "leaf": {
                  "tag": "expression_statement",
                  "text": "b;"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "w": "}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "coparse": "{a;b;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "quote_with_cmds_and_hole",
      "term": {
        "quote": {
          "tag": "x",
          "index": 0,
          "lang": "py",
          "term": {
            "leaf": {
              "tag": "integer",
              "text": "5"
            }
          },
          "cmds": [
            {
              "write": "["
            },
            "HOLE",
            {
              "write": "]"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "coparse": "[5]"
    },
    {
      "name": "unquote_bare_hole",
      "term": {
        "unquote": {
          "tag": "x",
          "index": 1,
          "lang": "py",
          "term": {
            "leaf": {
              "tag": "integer",
              "text": "5"
            }
          },
          "cmds": [
            "HOLE"
          ]
        }
      },
      "coparse": "5"
    },
    {
      "name": "qlift_int",
      "term": {
        "qlift": 42
      },
      "coparse": "42"
    },
    {
      "name": "qlift_float",
      "term": {
        "qlift": 1.5
      },
      "coparse": "1.5"
    },
    {
      "name": "qlift_float_integral_keeps_its_point",
      "runtimes": [
        "rust",
        "python"
      ],
      "why": "1.0 formatted with to_string() is '1' in Rust, which would lift a float as an integer literal and silently change the generated code's type",
      "term": {
        "qlift": 1.0
      },
      "coparse": "1.0"
    },
    {
      "name": "qlift_float_integral_drops_its_point_in_ts",
      "runtimes": [
        "wasm"
      ],
      "why": "Deliberately different, and correct for the target: every JS number is a double, so `1` and `1.0` are the same value and `fmt_number` drops the point so whole numbers read as integer literals. The distinction only matters in a language with separate int and float types",
      "term": {
        "qlift": 1.0
      },
      "coparse": "1"
    },
    {
      "name": "qlift_bool",
      "runtimes": [
        "rust",
        "wasm"
      ],
      "why": "Rust and TypeScript both spell the literal `true`; Python spells it `True`, so that case is separate rather than pretending the three agree",
      "term": {
        "qlift": true
      },
      "coparse": "true"
    },
    {
      "name": "qlift_bool_python_spelling",
      "runtimes": [
        "python"
      ],
      "why": "Python's boolean literal is `True`. This case exists because the runtime used to return `1`: bool is an int subclass, so extract::<i64> matched first and silently generated an integer where the author wrote a boolean",
      "term": {
        "qlift": true
      },
      "coparse": "True"
    },
    {
      "name": "qlift_string",
      "term": {
        "qlift": "hi"
      },
      "coparse": "\"hi\""
    },
    {
      "name": "qlift_string_with_quote",
      "term": {
        "qlift": "a\"b"
      },
      "coparse": "\"a\\\"b\"",
      "why": "the escaping bug #144 found in QLift for str: a bare `\"` produced a literal that does not reparse"
    },
    {
      "name": "qlift_string_with_backslash",
      "term": {
        "qlift": "a\\b"
      },
      "coparse": "\"a\\\\b\""
    },
    {
      "name": "qlift_on_term_identity_DEVIATION",
      "runtimes": [
        "python"
      ],
      "why": "records current quilt-python behaviour, which is wrong — see `deviation`",
      "term": {
        "qlift": {
          "leaf": {
            "tag": "integer",
            "text": "7"
          }
        }
      },
      "coparse": "7",
      "deviation": "Violates ↓(↑(x)) == x. Python returns the term unchanged, so ↓ then evaluates the term's own code (`7`) instead of reconstructing the term. Pinned to make a change visible; the fix is issue #166 and is breaking for a published package."
    },
    {
      "name": "qlift_on_term_builds_constructor_code",
      "runtimes": [
        "rust"
      ],
      "why": "The correct behaviour under ↓(↑(x)) == x: evaluating the lifted code reconstructs the term. Rust is the reference here; issue #166 tracks bringing python and wasm into line.",
      "term": {
        "qlift": {
          "leaf": {
            "tag": "integer_literal",
            "text": "7"
          }
        }
      },
      "coparse": "leaf(\"integer_literal\", \"7\")"
    },
    {
      "name": "qlift_html_int",
      "runtimes": [
        "python",
        "wasm"
      ],
      "why": "no LiftTo<Html> marker exists on the Rust side — issue #149",
      "term": {
        "qlift_html": 42
      },
      "coparse": "42"
    },
    {
      "name": "qlift_html_escapes_markup",
      "runtimes": [
        "python",
        "wasm"
      ],
      "why": "no LiftTo<Html> marker exists on the Rust side — issue #149",
      "term": {
        "qlift_html": "a \"<b>\" & c"
      },
      "coparse": "a &quot;&lt;b&gt;&quot; &amp; c"
    },
    {
      "name": "qlift_html_is_idempotent_on_terms",
      "runtimes": [
        "python",
        "wasm"
      ],
      "why": "no LiftTo<Html> marker exists on the Rust side — issue #149",
      "term": {
        "qlift_html": {
          "leaf": {
            "tag": "text",
            "text": "x"
          }
        }
      },
      "coparse": "x"
    },
    {
      "name": "deep_nesting",
      "term": {
        "tb": {
          "tag": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "c": {
                "tb": {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "steps": [
                    {
                      "c": {
                        "tb": {
                          "tag": "c",
                          "steps": [
                            {
                              "c": {
                                "leaf": {
                                  "tag": "d",
                                  "text": "deep"
                                }
                              }
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "coparse": "deep"
    },
    {
      "name": "unicode_content_survives",
      "term": {
        "leaf": {
          "tag": "string_content",
          "text": "héllo ← ↖ 世界"
        }
      },
      "coparse": "héllo ← ↖ 世界",
      "why": "the runtime must not apply Quilt's own glyph escaping to target text"
    }
  ]
